  "PROOF": "Exact core-zero cap T<=255 for 65555555555550000000 on the frozen seven-row authority.\n\nSupport model (r5 at 6569a966). Twenty tickets carry six labels each: 22 labels have\ntriple supports and 27 have pair supports. Every 2-subset of every support is distinct,\nso two tickets share at most one label, G (shadow plus pairs) has 66+27=93 edges and\ndeg(v)=2d_v+(6-d_v)=6+d_v, where d_v counts the triples through v. T=t(G), the 22 support\ntriangles included.\n\nPremises. d=(6,5^12,0^7): sum d=66, sum d^2=336, core K={d>0} with k=13, zeros Z with\nz=7. This is the core-13/zero-7 type (as the T256/T257 rows), not a core-14/zero-6 type,\nand its Goodman constant is 297 (T256: 298, T257: 299), so the identity is re-derived\nhere. A triple through a zero would give it d>0, so all 22 triples lie in K and a core\nx reaches Z only through its 6-d_x pair labels: sigma_x=|N_G(x)&Z|<=6-d_x, i.e. 0 at the\nhub (d=6) and {0,1} at d=5. A zero has degree 6, so 0<=zeta_u=|N_G(u)&K|<=6. Both sums\ncount the K-Z edges of G: r=sum sigma=sum zeta.\n\nGoodman. H is the complement: |E(H)|=190-93=97, deg_H=13-d. Counting vertex triples by\ntheir H-edges gives t(G)=C(20,3)-18|E(H)|+sum C(13-d,2)-t(H)=1140-1746+903-t(H)\n=297-t(H). Goodman's C(20,3)-sum deg_G*deg_H/2=1140-843 agrees.\n\nMixed-triangle identity. Put M=H[K], MZ=H[Z]: deg_M(x)=h_x=6-d_x+sigma_x and\ndeg_MZ(u)=zeta_u. An H triangle lies in K, lies in Z, or has exactly one same-part edge.\nOver an M edge xy its Z apices number z-sigma_x-sigma_y+c_Z(xy), c_Z(xy)=|N_G(x)&N_G(y)&Z|;\nover an MZ edge uw its K apices number k-zeta_u-zeta_w+c_K(uw). Summing,\n t(H)=z|M|+k|MZ|-sum sigma*h-sum zeta^2+P,  P=t(M)+t(MZ)+sum_M c_Z+sum_MZ c_K.\nP is a sum of four cardinalities, so P>=0. Sum h=12+r, so |M|=(12+r)/2, |MZ|=r/2 and\nz|M|+k|MZ|=42+10r. Per coordinate sigma*h is 0 at the hub and sigma(1+sigma)=2 sigma on\n{0,1}, so sum sigma*h=2r. Hence\n t(H)=42+8r-sum zeta^2+P  and  T=255-8r+sum zeta^2-P.\n\nCap. zeta^2<=6 zeta on {0..6}, so\n T<=255-8r+6r-P=255-2r-P<=255\nfor every legal support structure. No graphicality, sampling or enumeration is used.\nSeparable form: with -8r=-2 sum sigma-6 sum zeta, T+P=255+sum sigma(sigma+2-d)\n+sum zeta(zeta-6), and each coordinate term is <=0 on its legal range. Equality needs\nr=0 and P=0. r=0 forces every zeta to 0, so MZ is empty and M is the perfect matching\n{h=1} on the twelve d=5 tickets, whence P=0 by itself: T=255 exactly when r=0.\n\nAttainment. Hub triples {0,2i-1,2i}; 16 triples on 1..12 that pack K12 minus the hub\nmatching and minus the 12-cycle L=1-3-5-7-9-11-2-4-6-8-10-12; the six alternate L edges\nas core pair labels; K7 on the zeros. That structure is legal with r=0, so T=255 is\nattained and 255 is the exact profile maximum. The witness is supplemental, not proof.\n\nRoute B. The frozen R32 envelope at the row's S4 base 1680 is recounted from scratch\n(S1, S2, the S3 path/pure/support weights, the K4 floor and A_MAX), with exact\nrationals, and must equal the r32 and split implementations term by term. Its domain is\n22<=T<=277=floor(W/3) with W=831 (the wedge identity needs W-3T>=0; the frozen engine\nrefuses T=278), tighter than the bare Goodman cap t(H)>=0, T<=297. The terms increase\nstrictly in T (step >= 8768), so each cap's envelope peaks at the cap. Cap 264\nreproduces the recorded row bound 313396120; cap 255 gives 313315656 (K4 420, A_MAX\n200, S4 238980, S3 5062176). Strict reduction needs cap<=263, the cursor 313394584\nneeds cap<=263, and the incumbent 313263888 needs cap<=249.\n\nLedger. 6569a966 is pinned by tree and by the seven-row result digest. The six-row\nreplay (83ddad7a pins) plus the sealed seventh update must reproduce the frozen\nseven-row ledger digest for digest; the target row is read from it, unchanged. Nothing\nis installed: no family gain is claimed. Global K20 optimality is unknown. No solver or\nsearch is run.\n",
